data: {"type": "thinking", "id": "t2", "content": "Now I have the full document. Let me analyze it and create an improved version. The user wants:\n1. Sharper writing\n2. Better formatting/look\n3. New sections if necessary\n4. More content on Hightouch (most important competitor)\n\nLet me also check their memory for any relevant context, and get the authentic voice guidelines since I'll be writing content.\n\nActually, for a competitor analysis document, I don't necessarily need authentic voice guidelines - that's more for brand content. But the document needs to be well-written and professional.\n\nLet me plan the improved document:\n\n**Structure:**\n1. Executive Summary\n2. Competitor Analyses (HubSpot, Salesforce Agentforce, Hightouch - expanded, 6sense, Claude)\n\n\n3. Cross-Competitor Patterns / Key Themes\n4. US vs EU Website Conventions\n5. Recommendations for DOJO AI\n\nFor Hightouch, I need to expand significantly since it's the most important competitor. I should dig into what I know about them - they're a Composable CDP focused on data activation, syncing data from warehouses to marketing tools, with AI decisioning capabilities built in. Their positioning has shifted toward \"AI Decisioning\" as a core feature, which is directly relevant to DOJO AI's space.\n\nI should pull their actual website to get current, accurate details rather than relying on general knowledge. I'm also thinking about what would make this analysis most useful - a comparison matrix showing how each competitor positions themselves, a breakdown of their CTAs, and then consolidated DOJO-specific recommendations based on all the patterns I'm seeing."}

