data: {"type": "action", "id": "act14", "icon": "notebook", "title": "Coding", "results": [], "results_units": "Results", "started_at": "2026-08-01T09:13:57.612676Z", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T09:14:30.996195Z", "input": {"source": "\n# --- 6sense ---\nadd_heading2(doc, \"4. 6sense\")\nthreat_label(doc, \"Medium\", (0xC0, 0x80, 0x00))\nadd_table_2col(doc, [\n    (\"Headline\", '\"Signals Tell You What. We Tell You Why. Wherever You GTM.\"'),\n    (\"Headline Style\", \"Insight-led, confident, slightly abstract, category-defining\"),\n    (\"Primary CTA\", \"Get a Demo\"),\n    (\"Secondary CTA\", \"Watch Overview\"),\n])\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Core Value Proposition\")\nadd_body(doc, '\"Turn buyer signals into actionable intelligence that drives revenue across your go-to-market strategy.\" The message targets a specific pain point: companies have access to fragmented buyer signals but struggle to interpret them or prioritise accounts. 6sense positions itself as the interpretation layer that turns data noise into decision clarity.')\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Messaging Themes\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Primary: Buyer signals\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Secondary: Revenue intelligence\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Supporting: GTM alignment, predictive insight, account prioritisation, decision-making clarity\")\nadd_heading3(doc, \"What They Do Well\")\nadd_body(doc, \"6sense has genuine category ownership in revenue intelligence for B2B GTM teams. The headline is memorable precisely because it creates a tension ('signals tell you what, we tell you why') that implies a gap in what existing tools provide. This is strong category-creation copywriting: name the limitation of the status quo, then position your product as the answer.\")\nadd_body(doc, 'The \"why\" framing is also strategically sharp. In a market flooded with tools that show more data, 6sense claims to be the one that explains what it means — a meaningful differentiator for an executive buyer drowning in dashboards.')\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Where They Fall Short\")\nadd_body(doc, '\"Wherever You GTM\" assumes the reader already knows GTM terminology and thinks in those terms. For a broader or less B2B-native audience, this can read as jargon.')\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Key Lessons for DOJO\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Position DOJO as an interpretation and action layer, not just a data surface or automation tool. 'We tell you why' is a useful framing principle.\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"The value DOJO creates is clarity plus execution — a stronger claim than either alone.\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Creating tension in a headline ('you have signals but not understanding') is a powerful copywriting technique worth borrowing.\")\nadd_hr(doc)\n\n# --- Claude ---\nadd_heading2(doc, \"5. Claude (Anthropic)\")\nthreat_label(doc, \"High (indirect)\", (0xC0, 0x30, 0x30))\nadd_table_2col(doc, [\n    (\"Headline\", '\"Meet Claude.\" / \"Your AI assistant for thinking, writing and coding.\"'),\n    (\"Headline Style\", \"Minimal, human, product-led\"),\n    (\"Primary CTA\", \"Try Claude\"),\n    (\"Secondary CTA\", \"Learn More\"),\n])\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Core Value Proposition\")\nadd_body(doc, '\"A helpful, reliable AI assistant for thinking, writing, analysis, and coding.\" Claude targets knowledge workers who spend significant time on cognitive tasks and want to reduce that effort. The value proposition is broad and deliberately non-industry-specific.')\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Messaging Themes\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Primary: Intelligence and reasoning\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Secondary: Productivity and writing support\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Supporting: Safety, clarity, trust, accessibility\")\nadd_heading3(doc, \"What They Do Well\")\nadd_body(doc, \"Claude's website is the clearest example in this analysis of minimal-cognitive-load design. There are no bold transformation claims, no enterprise jargon, no multi-pillar product frameworks. The site removes every barrier between the visitor and understanding what the product does. The emphasis on trust and safety is well-executed: in a world of AI anxiety, calm and confident messaging about reliability is a meaningful differentiator.\")\nadd_body(doc, 'The friction-free CTA (\"Try Claude\") is notably lower-commitment than any other competitor in this analysis. This reflects their consumer-facing model, but the principle — make the first action easy — applies universally.')\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Where They Are Weaker (as a reference point for DOJO)\")\nadd_body(doc, \"Claude's deliberate generality is both its strength and its limitation. Because it serves everyone, it cannot claim to be the expert system for any specific domain. DOJO's specificity — 'built for marketing teams, grounded in your brand's actual history' — is a structural advantage over general-purpose AI tools. The risk DOJO faces from Claude is not direct substitution; it is the buyer who thinks 'I already have Claude, why do I need DOJO?' DOJO's website needs to make the answer to that question obvious and immediate.\")\nadd_heading3(doc, \"Key Lessons for DOJO\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Clarity is not the enemy of depth. Claude proves you can be extremely clear and still be credible.\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"Avoid overcomplicating messaging above the fold. If a first-time visitor cannot understand DOJO's value in five seconds, the site is doing too much work.\")\nadd_bullet(doc, \"DOJO should not compete with general AI tools on capabilities. The differentiator is specificity: DOJO knows your brand. Claude does not know anything about your brand.\")\n\ndoc.add_page_break()\n\nprint(\"6sense + Claude done\")\n"}}

event: final
