data: {"type": "action", "id": "act19", "icon": "file-pen", "title": "Updating DOJO Website Competitor Analysis", "results": [], "started_at": "2026-08-01T11:16:59.549555Z", "ended_at": "2026-08-01T11:17:26.046135Z", "input": {"path": "outputs/DOJO Website Competitor Analysis.md", "content": "# DOJO AI: Competitor Website Analysis\n*Messaging, Positioning, and Website Strategy Lessons — June 2026*\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nBest-in-class competitor websites lead with outcomes, build trust fast, and save technical depth for lower on the page. DOJO should do the same.\n\nCritical flag: Hightouch has pivoted from a data-platform identity to \"Agentic Marketing Platform\" — directly into DOJO's positioning territory. The distinction needs to be explicit on DOJO's site.\n\n---\n\n## Competitor Profiles\n\n---\n\n### 1. HubSpot\n**Threat Level: High**\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Headline** | \"Where go-to-market teams go to grow.\" |\n| **Primary CTA** | Get Started |\n| **Secondary CTA** | Get a Demo |\n\n**Strengths**\n- Outcome-first: the headline is about growth, not product or AI\n- Zero jargon above the fold\n- Trust established before any product explanation\n\n**Lessons for DOJO**\n- Lead with the outcome (growth, clarity, efficiency), not the mechanism\n- One message above the fold — everything else below\n\n---\n\n### 2. Salesforce Agentforce\n**Threat Level: Medium**\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Headline** | \"Deploy autonomous AI agents to support your employees and customers 24/7.\" |\n| **Primary CTA** | Watch Demo |\n| **Secondary CTA** | Start Building |\n\n**Strengths**\n- Created a new category rather than describing a feature\n- AI framed as an active operator, not a passive tool\n- Trust and governance addressed in the headline itself\n\n**Lessons for DOJO**\n- Own \"intelligent marketing system\" as a category — don't compete inside someone else's\n- Frame DOJO's agents as operators, not assistants\n\n---\n\n### 3. Hightouch\n**Threat Level: High (Priority Competitor)**\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Headline** | \"Marketing looks different here.\" |\n| **Subheadline** | \"Go from insight to live campaign in minutes – powered by all your data, brand knowledge, and AI.\" |\n| **Primary CTA** | Get a Demo |\n\n> **Important:** Hightouch has dropped their \"Composable CDP\" identity and relaunched as an **Agentic Marketing Platform**. They now claim brand-aware AI, fast campaign execution, and agentic insights — the same territory as DOJO.\n\n**Platform (June 2026)**\n\n| Pillar | Modules |\n|---|---|\n| Agentic Marketing Platform *(new)* | Ad Studio, Content Assembly, AI Decisioning, Intelligence |\n| Composable CDP *(foundation)* | Customer Studio, Reverse ETL, Identity Resolution, Real-time Personalisation, Match Booster, Events |\n\n300+ integrations. Gartner MQ Leader (CDP, Jan 2026). Customers: Spotify, Warner Music Group, Domino's, PetSmart, Grammarly, DoorDash.\n\n**Strengths**\n- Household-name logos immediately below the hero; awards mid-page\n- Concrete proof points: *\"Otrium cuts campaign launch time by 70%, drives 15% more conversions\"*\n- Four-stage execution narrative: Explore → Audiences → Campaigns → Ads\n- Security featured mid-page, not buried in the footer\n\n**Weaknesses**\n- Headline is emotive but says nothing — a cold visitor won't know what Hightouch does\n- Dual-product structure (AMP + CDP) creates cognitive friction\n- Trying to serve data teams and marketing teams simultaneously dilutes both messages\n- \"Agentic Marketing Platform\" is a description, not a category\n\n**Lessons for DOJO**\n- Draw the line clearly on the website: *Hightouch activates data. DOJO accumulates intelligence.*\n- Replace logo walls with outcome metrics\n- Consider a similar end-to-end execution narrative\n- Establish the CDP distinction before Hightouch blurs it further\n\n---\n\n### 4. 6sense\n**Threat Level: Medium**\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Headline** | \"Signals Tell You What. We Tell You Why. Wherever You GTM.\" |\n| **Primary CTA** | Get a Demo |\n| **Secondary CTA** | Watch Overview |\n\n**Strengths**\n- Clear category ownership in revenue intelligence\n- Headline names the gap in the status quo, then positions the product as the answer\n- \"We tell you why\" cuts through a market drowning in dashboards\n\n**Lessons for DOJO**\n- Position DOJO as interpretation and action, not just automation\n- Tension-based headlines (\"you have data but not understanding\") are worth borrowing\n\n---\n\n### 5. Claude (Anthropic)\n**Threat Level: High (indirect)**\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Headline** | \"Meet Claude. Your AI assistant for thinking, writing and coding.\" |\n| **Primary CTA** | Try Claude |\n\n**Strengths**\n- Minimal friction: one message, no jargon, no product frameworks\n- Lowest-commitment CTA in this analysis\n- Trust through simplicity and calm, not feature lists\n\n**Lessons for DOJO**\n- Clarity and credibility are not in conflict\n- The \"why not just use Claude?\" objection needs a direct answer on DOJO's site: *generic AI knows nothing about your brand. DOJO does.*\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Competitor Snapshot\n\n| Competitor | Primary Hook | AI Positioning | Trust Mechanism | CTA |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| HubSpot | Growth | Enabler | Scale, simplicity | Get Started |\n| Salesforce | AI Agents | The product | Brand authority | Demo |\n| Hightouch | Execution speed | Brand-aware AI | Gartner, logos, metrics | Demo |\n| 6sense | Buyer intelligence | Interpreter | Category ownership | Demo |\n| Claude | Thinking/writing | Calm assistant | Safety, simplicity | Try |\n| **DOJO** | **Compounding intelligence** | **AI that learns your brand** | **Graph + loop** | **TBD** |\n\n---\n\n## US vs. EU Website Conventions\n\n| | US | EU |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Messaging** | Short, outcome-first, no jargon | Detailed, technically specific |\n| **Above the fold** | One headline, one CTA | More content, more explanation |\n| **Trust** | Brand authority, social proof | Rigour and product depth |\n| **CTA** | Low-friction (\"Try free\") | Higher-commitment (\"Request demo\") |\n\n**DOJO's approach:** US clarity at the top, EU depth as you scroll.\n\n> *Simple enough to understand in 5 seconds. Deep enough to believe in 5 minutes.*\n\n- **Above the fold:** one outcome, one category claim, one CTA\n- **Mid-page:** the compounding loop (input → graph → agents → outcome → feedback)\n- **Lower page:** logos with metrics, case studies, technical depth, trust signals\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations\n\n| # | Action |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | **Own the category.** \"The intelligent marketing system\" should be the first thing every visitor sees. |\n| 2 | **Show what compounding produces, not how it works.** Sharper decisions, a system that improves over time. |\n| 3 | **Draw the Hightouch line.** *Hightouch activates data. DOJO accumulates intelligence.* |\n| 4 | **Replace logo walls with outcome metrics.** Specific results, not just names. |\n| 5 | **Simplify above the fold.** One headline, one subheadline, one CTA. |\n| 6 | **Explain the loop visually.** Data in → graph builds → agents act → outcomes feed back → system learns. |\n| 7 | **Answer the Claude objection.** Generic AI knows nothing about your brand. DOJO does. |\n\n---\n\n*Prepared by DOJO AI intern team, June 2026.*\n", "overwrite": true}, "kind": "library"}

event: final
